IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P9-art-81: Article 81, "Union safeguard procedure" (consolidated text of 27.7.2026; unchanged by the Omnibus).
-- Group General (2 August 2026). Every function takes `the date asked` first and the AI system the procedure is about;
-- before the group applies, or where Article 111(2) saves the system, the answer is NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
-- The Commission, the market surveillance authorities and the Member States are officials: they have no seat. The operator
-- (a provider, deployer, importer, distributor, authorised representative or product manufacturer) is consulted (paragraph 1)
-- and may be made to withdraw its AI system from the markets of all Member States (paragraph 2): the seats ask both.
-- Periods: "three months", "30 days", "six months" and "60 days" are counted from the date of the notification
-- referred to in Article 79(5): three and six months with `add months` (the same day of the month, clamped), days by adding them.
-- The count (the day of the notification itself is not counted) is assumed, not ruled: fork F-81-count.
-- Seams: the notification of Article 79(5) is an input (its date); whether the non-compliance is with the prohibition of Article 5
-- is the seam S3 (an input).

§ `Seam S14: the reference each provision gives to Article 2(2)`

-- Article 2(2): for a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in
-- Section B of Annex I, "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply". The keel asks of a provision by its Article
-- number, letter and paragraph; paragraph 0 would mean the whole Article. Each function below that is about an AI system asks it of its own paragraph.

`Art 81(1) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 81
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 1

`Art 81(2) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 81
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 2

`Art 81(3) reference to the provision` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
    number IS 81
    letter IS ""
    paragraph IS 3

§ `Article 81: the parties and the acts`

DECLARE `Art 81 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 81 the Commission`
    `Art 81 a Member State`

DECLARE `Art 81 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 81(1) enter into consultation with the market surveillance authority of the relevant Member State and the operator or operators, and evaluate the national measure`
    `Art 81(1) decide whether the national measure is justified`
    `Art 81(1) notify the decision to the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned and inform all other market surveillance authorities of it`
    `Art 81(2) take appropriate restrictive measures in respect of the AI system concerned and inform the Commission`
    `Art 81(2) withdraw the national measure and inform the Commission`
    `Art 81(3) apply the procedure provided for in Article 11 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`

§ `Article 81(1): the periods, counted from the notification referred to in Article 79(5)`

-- src:1326 | 1. Where, within three months of receipt of the notification referred to in Article 79(5), or within 30 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5, objections are raised by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority, or where the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law, the Commission shall without undue delay enter into consultation with the market surveillance authority of the relevant Member State and the operator or operators, and shall evaluate the national measure. On the basis of the results of that evaluation, the Commission shall, within six months, or within 60 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5, starting from the notification referred to in Article 79(5), decide whether the national measure is justified and shall notify its decision to the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned. The Commission shall also inform all other market surveillance authorities of its decision.
@ref Art 81(1) (src:1326)
GIVEN `the date of receipt of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` IS A DATE
      `the case is non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 81(1) the last day on which an objection can be raised` MEANS
    IF `the case is non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`
    THEN `the date of receipt of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` PLUS 30  -- "within 30 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5"
    ELSE `add months` `the date of receipt of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` 3  -- "within three months of receipt of the notification"

@ref Art 81(1)
GIVEN `the date of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` IS A DATE
      `the case is non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 81(1) the last day on which the Commission can decide` MEANS
    IF `the case is non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`
    THEN `the date of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` PLUS 60  -- "within 60 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5, starting from the notification"
    ELSE `add months` `the date of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` 6  -- "within six months ... starting from the notification"

§ `Article 81(1): consultation and evaluation by the Commission`

@ref Art 81(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an objection was raised, within the period, by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1) the Commission must enter into consultation and evaluate the national measure` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 81(1) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) as amended: "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply"); this provision is not among them (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE IF       `an objection was raised, within the period, by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority`
                    OR `the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law`
              THEN JUST TRUE  -- "without undue delay": the text gives no number of days
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, within three months ..., objections are raised by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority, or where the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law" (a "where" condition that is not met)

@ref Art 81(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an objection was raised, within the period, by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 81 party` `Art 81 act`
`Art 81(1) the duty of the Commission to consult the market surveillance authority and the operator and to evaluate the national measure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 81(1) the Commission must enter into consultation and evaluate the national measure` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `an objection was raised, within the period, by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority` `the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 81 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 81(1) enter into consultation with the market surveillance authority of the relevant Member State and the operator or operators, and evaluate the national measure`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- The Commission's decision: "within six months, or within 60 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices
-- referred to in Article 5, starting from the notification referred to in Article 79(5)". The rule arises when the Commission has to evaluate the national measure.
@ref Art 81(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has to evaluate the national measure under Article 81(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` IS A DATE
      `the case is non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 81 party` `Art 81 act`
`Art 81(1) the duty of the Commission to decide whether the national measure is justified` MEANS
    IF       `Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`
         AND NOT (`Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 81(1) reference to the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE)  -- Article 2(2): this Article is not among those that apply to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach); the other answers leave the duty to its own provision
         AND `the Commission has to evaluate the national measure under Article 81(1)`
    THEN PARTY `Art 81 the Commission`
         MUST `Art 81(1) decide whether the national measure is justified`
         WITHIN (Day (`Art 81(1) the last day on which the Commission can decide` `the date of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)` `the case is non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`)) MINUS (Day `the date of the notification referred to in Article 79(5)`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 81 the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not decide whether the national measure is justified within six months, or within 60 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5, starting from the notification referred to in Article 79(5)"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

